[#:seon.task{:name "a-deftest-reply-shows-only-its-var"
             :kind :function
             :intent "Entering a deftest at the REPL answers #'ns/test-name and nothing else: no run, no pass/fail, no pending marker and no next operation, so the agent learns whether its regression is red or green only by proposing (dogfood loop 2026-09-28, loop 1: the proof's first verdict arrived 7 s later inside propose-merge!'s refusal). The Var render of a test shows its status at its current reach digest (green, red with the first failing assertion, or pending) and offers the run of exactly that test, as the defn Var render shows reaching-test status."
             :must-read #{seon.render.var/status}
             :evidence #{"docs/research/agent-platform/dogfood-loop-2026-09-28.md"}}
 #:seon.task{:name "reaching-tests-are-never-run-and-a-first-red-is-silent"
             :kind :function
             :intent "The namespace docstring says a definition's batch schedules its reaching tests, but no pass does: the only callers of seon.test/run are my.test/check, my.test/run-owned, my.program/propose-merge! and root's candidate gate. Redefining a function reached by a test leaves status answering :pending across later passes with no member row. After an explicit my.test/check records that test red, status answers {} because a red with no earlier result is neither pending nor newly red, so the agent is never shown its red test. The pass schedules the reaching tests off the pass (agent-loop spec 4.5, AR-01) and status names a first red (AR-04)."
             :must-read #{seon.render.var/status}
             :evidence #{"docs/seon/specs/agent-loop.md"}}]
